<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Validation of the Maximum Generation Length</h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluation includes models specifically designed for long Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning, such as QwQ-32B, Gemini-2.5-pro and DeepSeek-R1. For these models, a methodological concern is that their inherently verbose reasoning might consume a disproportionate share of the 1024-token generation limit, leaving insufficient space for the final answer. To investigate this, we conduct a validation experiment in both single-turn and multi-turn settings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T10" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:60%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Performance comparison of QwQ-32B and QwQ-32B-2048. White and gray rows indicate the single-turn and multi-turn setting, respectively.</figcaption>
